+# CONTRACT — Permission Maze Document Management API
+
+## Auth
+- [x] `POST /auth/register` with `{username, password}` creates a user → 201, returns `{id, username}` (no password). Test: register, assert 201 + body shape.
+- [x] `POST /auth/register` missing username/password → 400. Test: omit field, assert 400.
+- [x] `POST /auth/register` duplicate username → 409. Test: register twice with same username.
+- [x] `POST /auth/login` with correct credentials → 200, returns `{token}`. Test: login after register, assert 200 + token string.
+- [x] `POST /auth/login` with wrong password / unknown user → 401. Test: bad password, assert 401.
+- [x] Protected routes without `Authorization: Bearer <token>` → 401. Test: call `POST /folders` with no header.
+- [x] Protected routes with invalid/garbage token → 401. Test: call with `Bearer bogus`.
+
+## Folders
+- [x] `POST /folders` with `{name}` (no parent) → 201, creator becomes owner. Test: assert role owner via subsequent GET.
+- [x] `POST /folders` with `{name, parentId}` where parentId valid and creator has ≥editor → 201, nested correctly.
+- [x] `POST /folders` with nonexistent `parentId` → 404.
+- [x] `POST /folders` with `parentId` the user can't edit → 403.
+- [x] `POST /folders` missing/empty `name` → 400.
+- [x] `GET /folders/:id` as owner → 200 full folder.
+- [x] `GET /folders/:id` as user with no access → 403.
+- [x] `GET /folders/:id` nonexistent id → 404.
+- [x] `PUT /folders/:id` rename as owner/editor → 200 updated.
+- [x] `PUT /folders/:id` as viewer-only → 403.
+- [x] `PUT /folders/:id` moving into a descendant of itself (cycle) → 400.
+- [x] `DELETE /folders/:id` as owner → 204, folder + nested subfolders + documents removed.
+- [x] `DELETE /folders/:id` as editor (not owner) → 403.
+
+## Documents
+- [x] `POST /folders/:folderId/documents` with `{title, content}` as editor/owner of folder → 201, creator is document owner.
+- [x] `POST /folders/:folderId/documents` as viewer-only of folder → 403.
+- [x] `POST /folders/:folderId/documents` nonexistent folder → 404.
+- [x] `GET /documents/:id` as viewer → 200.
+- [x] `GET /documents/:id` no access → 403.
+- [x] `GET /documents/:id` nonexistent → 404.
+- [x] `PUT /documents/:id` as editor → 200 updated, `updatedAt` changes.
+- [x] `PUT /documents/:id` as viewer-only → 403.
+- [x] `DELETE /documents/:id` as owner → 204.
+- [x] `DELETE /documents/:id` as editor (not owner) → 403.
+- [x] User with editor on parent folder (no direct doc share) can read/edit a document inside it (inheritance). Test directly.
+
+## Sharing & permission resolution
+- [x] `POST /folders/:id/share` `{userId, role}` by owner → 200/201, target user gains role.
+- [x] `POST /documents/:id/share` `{userId, role}` by owner → 200/201.
+- [x] Sharing by a user with only viewer permission → 403.
+- [x] Editor can share viewer/editor roles but cannot grant `owner` role → 403 when editor attempts role=owner.
+- [x] Sharing with invalid role string → 400.
+- [x] Sharing targeting nonexistent user → 404.
+- [x] Effective permission = most permissive across direct share + inherited folder share. Test: user has viewer via folder share and editor via direct document share → effective editor (can PUT the doc).
+- [x] `DELETE /folders/:id/share/:userId` and `/documents/:id/share/:userId` by owner revokes access → 200/204, subsequent GET by that user → 403.
+
+## Activity Log
+- [x] `GET /activity` requires auth → 401 without token.
+- [x] Creating a document logs an entry with `{action, actorId, targetType, targetId, timestamp}`.
+- [x] Updating/deleting a document logs entries.
+- [x] Sharing logs an entry.
+- [x] Activity entries are visible to the actor.
+- [x] Log entries appear most-recent-first.
+
+## Build/Lint/Test
+- [x] `npm run build` succeeds with no TS errors.
+- [x] `npm run lint` passes with no errors.
+- [x] `npm test` — all tests pass.
